cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this chip design, firmware, data, or plotting code, please cite the
  design deposit below.
title: "OSCAR: Open-Silicon Chemosensing Analog RISC-V array"
abstract: >-
  Design sources, RISC-V firmware, host bridge, archived datasets and plotting
  scripts for a SkyWater 130-nm Caravel/Caravan neuromorphic chemosensing chip:
  a TiO2-coated electrode pad and capacitively coupled LNA feeding sixteen analog
  leaky-integrate-and-fire neurons with 512 4-bit DPI synapses, managed end to end
  by a VexRiscv RV32I core over a four-phase address-event interface.
